    Let $(X, \preceq)$ be a partially ordered set. Then, the minimum sorting map $\varsigma_{\mathrm{min}}:\mathscr{T}(X) \to \mathscr{S}(X,\preceq)$ defined by sorting each comparability component separately and concatenating the results is an idempotent sorting map.
