\begin{cor}\label{cor:tuple-space-covered-by-sorting-valid-elements}
     Let $(X, \preceq)$ be a partially ordered set and $\mathscr{T}(X)$ the associated tuple space. Then for every $\bm{x}\in \mathscr{T}(X)$ there exists a $\pi \in \mathscr{P}$ such that 
