proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
    For each $\alpha \in \{\oplus,\ominus,\circledast\}$, the restriction of $\lhd$ to $\mathscr{T}(X)\times (F_\alpha\times\{\alpha\})$ is exactly the corresponding primitive action map. By Theorem~\ref{thm:analytic-properties-actions}, each of these restricted maps is continuous. The canonical identification $\mathscr{T}(X)\times\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in A}(F_\alpha\times\{\alpha\})\cong\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in A}\bigl(\mathscr{T}(X)\times F_\alpha\times\{\alpha\}\bigr)$ is a homeomorphism, because every disjoint-union component is open. Hence the continuity of $\lhd$ follows from the pasting lemma for disjoint unions (Theorem~\ref{thm:pasting-lemma}).
\end{proof}

