\begin{proof}
    Note that since $\mathfrak{I}$ is a measurable function with values in the countable set $\mathscr{F}(\mathbb{N}^2)$, endowed with the power set as its $\sigma$-algebra, the sets
    \begin{align*}
        \mathscr{U}_\eta =\{((\bm{Q}, \bm{p}), (\bm{Q}^\prime, \bm{p}^\prime)) \in \mathfrak{C}(\leq)\times \mathfrak{C}(\geq) \mid \mathfrak{I}(\bm{p},\bm{p}^\prime) = \eta\} 
    \end{align*}
    form a measurable partition of the domain. 

    Now, for each $\eta \in \mathscr{F}(\mathbb{N}^2)$ define the function $m_\eta: \mathscr{U}_\eta \to \mathbb{R}$ by
    \begin{align*}
        m_\eta((\bm{Q},\bm{p}), (\bm{Q}^\prime, \bm{p}^\prime)) = \begin{cases}
            0 & \eta = \emptyset\\
        \max_{(i,j)\in \eta} \min (\bm{Q}(i), \bm{Q}^\prime(j)) & \eta \neq \emptyset,
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    and note that $m_\eta$ is measurable on the subspace $\sigma$-algebra, as the coordinate maps 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathrm{ev}_i(\bm{x}) =  \begin{cases}
            0 & i \notin\mathrm{domain}(\bm{x})\\
            \bm{x}(i) & i \in \mathrm{domain}(\bm{x})
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    are continuous on every fixed-length layer, since on layers of length less than $i$ they are identically zero and on layers of length at least $i$ they are coordinate projections. The \hyperref[thm:the-standard-machinery]{standard machinery} therefore makes them continuous for the disjoint-layer tuple topology. Moreover, the maximum and minimum are continuous on $\mathbb{R}^2$, and as a result $m_\eta$ is measurable on $\mathscr{U}_\eta$. Finally, by construction, $\mathscr{Q}\restriction_{\mathscr{U}_\eta} = m_\eta$ for every $\eta \in \mathscr{F}(\mathbb{N}^2)$. Therefore, Theorem~\ref{thm:measurable-partition} yields that $\mathscr{Q}$ is measurable on the whole domain.
\end{proof}

