\begin{prop}\label{prop:function-kernel-quotient-injective-extension}
    Let $X$ and $Y$ be non-empty sets and $\varphi : X \to Y$ a function. Then, $\varphi$ induces a well-defined injective mapping $\Phi : X_\varphi \to Y$ such that, for every $x\in X$, $\Phi(x_\varphi) = \varphi(x)$.
\end{prop}

proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
    By Proposition~\ref{prop:phi-subspace}, the image $\varphi(X)$ is a subspace of $V$. By the preceding proposition, $\Phi:X_\varphi \to \varphi(X)$ is a bijection. The displayed formulas therefore define the pullback of addition and scalar multiplication on the vector space $\varphi(X)$ along the bijection $\Phi$. Consequently, all vector-space axioms on $X_\varphi$ follow immediately from the corresponding axioms on $\varphi(X)$.
\end{proof}

