proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
    By construction (Theorem~\ref{thm:weak-linear-transport-vector-space-structure}), $\Phi:X_\varphi\to\varphi(X)$ is a linear bijection, and
    \begin{align*}
        \llangle \vphantom{.}x_\varphi, x^\prime_\varphi \rrangle = \langle \vphantom{.}\Phi(x_\varphi), \Phi(x^\prime_\varphi) \rangle = \langle \varphi(x), \varphi(x^\prime)\rangle.
    \end{align*}
    Since $(V, \langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle)$ is an inner product space over $\mathbb{R}$, and the pullback of an inner product along an injective linear map is an inner product, the claim follows.
\end{proof}

