proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
    By Proposition~\ref{prop:function-kernel-quotient-injective-extension}, the map $\Phi:X_\varphi \to \varphi(X)$ is bijective, and by the definition of $\llangle\cdot,\cdot\rrangle$ it is an isometry between $(X_\varphi,\llangle\cdot,\cdot\rrangle)$ and the subspace $\varphi(X)$ of $\mathcal{H}$. Hence $(X_\varphi,\llangle\cdot,\cdot\rrangle)$ is complete if and only if $\varphi(X)$ is complete. A subspace of a Hilbert space is complete if and only if it is closed. Therefore the kernel space is a Hilbert space if and only if $\varphi(X)$ is closed.
\end{proof}

