\begin{defn}[Completed Kernel Space]\label{defn:completed-kernel-space}
    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $(\mathcal{H}, \langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle)$ a separable Hilbert space, and $\varphi : X \to \mathcal{H}$ a weakly linear operator. Let $(X_\varphi, \llangle \cdot , \cdot \rrangle)$ be the kernel space induced by $\varphi$. Then, we call the completion of $(X_\varphi, \llangle \cdot , \cdot \rrangle)$ the completed kernel space and denote it by
    \begin{align}
