    \begin{align*}
        \alpha x+\alpha z^\prime = \alpha x^\prime+\alpha z.
    \end{align*}
    Using compatibility of the transported cone structure with non-negative scalar multiplication, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \alpha x+\alpha z^\prime &= \alpha(x+z^\prime) \\
        &= \alpha(x^\prime+z) \\
        &= \alpha x^\prime+\alpha z.
    \end{align*}
