environments.rawEnvironment:
\begin{defn}[Excess Supply Function and Completed Graph]\label{defn:excess-supply-and-completed-graph}
    Let $\bm{m}\in\mathscr{T}(O)$ be a market state with supply curve $S^{\bm{m}}:[0,s_*]\to\mathcal{P}$ and demand curve $D^{\bm{m}}:[0,b_*]\to\mathcal{P}$, where $\mathcal{P}=[-500,\overline{p}]$. The \emph{excess supply function} $E^{\bm{m}}:\mathbb{R}\to[-b_*,s_*]$ is defined by
    \begin{align*}
        E^{\bm{m}}(p)
        &=\sup\bigl(\{0\}\cup\{q\in(0,s_*]\mid S^{\bm{m}}(q)\leq p\}\bigr)\\
        &\quad-\sup\bigl(\{0\}\cup\{q\in(0,b_*]\mid D^{\bm{m}}(q)\geq p\}\bigr).
    \end{align*}
    The \emph{completed graph} of $E^{\bm{m}}$ over $\mathcal{P}$ is the set of points $(p,e)\in\mathcal{P}\times\mathbb{R}$ satisfying $E^{\bm{m}}(p-)\leq e\leq E^{\bm{m}}(p+)$, and for each level $q\in[-b_*,s_*]$, the corresponding level set is
    \begin{align*}
        J_{\bm{m}}(q)=\bigl\{p\in\mathcal{P}\bigm| E^{\bm{m}}(p-)\leq q\leq E^{\bm{m}}(p+)\bigr\}.
    \end{align*}
\end{defn}

