\begin{prop}[Random Aggregated Curves and Hilbert-Valued Curves]\label{prop:pl-encoding-measurable}
    Fix $\overline{p}\in\{3000,4000\}$, and let $\mathcal{P}=[-500,\overline{p}]$. Let $\mathscr{L}$ be the set of pairs $\bm{m}=(\bm{s},\bm{b})\in\mathscr{T}(\mathbb{R}\times[0,\infty))\times\allowbreak\mathscr{T}(\mathbb{R}\times[0,\infty))$ of non-empty tuples whose first coordinates lie in $\mathcal{P}$, whose maximum first coordinate over both tuples equals $\overline{p}$, and whose maximum second coordinates are strictly positive in both tuples. Restrict $\mathscr{L}$ further to those pairs for which the construction below has strictly positive equilibrium quantity $Q(\bm{m})>0$, and endow $\mathscr{L}$ with the subspace metric inherited from the product of the tuple Hausdorff metrics. For each $\bm{m}\in\mathscr{L}$, let $P_{\bm{m}}:D_{\bm{m}}\to\mathcal{P}$ be the price-impact curve of Definition~\ref{defn:positively-matched-state-space-and-price-impact-curve} constructed from $\bm{s}$ and $\bm{b}$ after replacing the second coordinates of each tuple by their running maxima along the sorted orderings of increasing first coordinate for $\bm{s}$ and decreasing first coordinate for $\bm{b}$, and let $\overline{\Psi}:\mathpzc{P}\to L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2)$ denote the breakpoint-based sided parametrisation operator. Then the maps
    \begin{align*}
        \bm{m}\mapsto Z(\bm{m}):=\overline{\Psi}(P_{\bm{m}})\in L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2),\qquad \bm{m}\mapsto P_{\bm{m}}(0),
    \end{align*}
    are Borel measurable on $\mathscr{L}$. Moreover, if $\bm{M}$ is a measurable random element taking values in $\mathscr{L}$ and $D(\bm{M})=\max(b_*,s_*)$ denotes the larger of its terminal cumulative volumes, then $\mathbb{E}[D(\bm{M})^2]<\infty$ implies $\mathbb{E}[\lVert Z(\bm{M})\rVert_{L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2)}^2]<\infty$.
\end{prop}

