\begin{defn}[Lifted Scale Operator and Smearing Estimator]\label{defn:lifted-price-scale-smearing}
Let $c > 0$, let $g:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ be given by $g(p)=\operatorname{asinh}(p/c)$ with inverse $g^{-1}(z)=c\sinh(z)=c(\mathrm{e}^{z}-\mathrm{e}^{-z})/2$, and let $\operatorname{pr}_q,\operatorname{pr}_p:L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2)\to L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R})$ denote the first and second coordinate projections, respectively. The \emph{lifted scale operator} $\mathfrak{G}:L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2)\to L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2)$ is defined by
\begin{align*}
    \operatorname{pr}_q\mathfrak{G}f=\operatorname{pr}_qf,\qquad
    \operatorname{pr}_p\mathfrak{G}f=g\circ\operatorname{pr}_pf,
\end{align*}
which is well-defined since $|g(p)|\leq|p|/c$, and its inverse $\mathfrak{G}^{-1}$ on the subset of functions $h\in L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R}^2)$ with $g^{-1}\circ\operatorname{pr}_p h\in L^2([-1,1];\mathbb{R})$ is defined by
\begin{align*}
    \operatorname{pr}_q\mathfrak{G}^{-1}h=\operatorname{pr}_qh,\qquad
    \operatorname{pr}_p\mathfrak{G}^{-1}h=g^{-1}\circ\operatorname{pr}_ph.
\end{align*}
