proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
We establish the bound by rescaling an arbitrary feasible element of $\mathcal{A}_{\alpha\mathcal{G}}(\alpha q_{\mathrm{start}}, \alpha q_{\mathrm{stop}}; \widehat{\bm{P}}_d)$ and exploiting the monotonicity of $\widehat{P}_{d,h}$. Let $\Delta\bm{q} = (\Delta q_h)_{h=1}^{24} \in \mathcal{A}_{\alpha\mathcal{G}}(\alpha q_{\mathrm{start}}, \alpha q_{\mathrm{stop}}; \widehat{\bm{P}}_d)$, and define $\Delta\widetilde{\bm{q}} = \alpha^{-1}\Delta\bm{q}$. By construction, $\Delta\widetilde{q}_h \in \mathcal{R}$ and the cumulative sums satisfy $\widetilde{q}_h = q_{\mathrm{start}} + \sum_{r=1}^h \Delta\widetilde{q}_r = \alpha^{-1}q_h \in \mathcal{G}$ for all $h$, with $\widetilde{q}_{24} = q_{\mathrm{stop}}$. Moreover, because $\tau$ is positively homogeneous of degree one, $\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h) = \alpha^{-1}\tau(\Delta q_h)$ lies between $0$ and $\tau(\Delta q_h)$, and hence belongs to the interval $\operatorname{domain}(\widehat{P}_{d,h})$. Thus $\Delta\widetilde{\bm{q}} \in \mathcal{A}_{\mathcal{G}}(q_{\mathrm{start}}, q_{\mathrm{stop}}; \widehat{\bm{P}}_d)$.

Next, fix $h \in \{1,\dots,24\}$. Since $\alpha > 1$ and $\widehat{P}_{d,h}$ is non-decreasing, if $\tau(\Delta q_h) \geq 0$, then $0 \leq \tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h) \leq \tau(\Delta q_h)$ implies $\widehat{P}_{d,h}(\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h)) \leq \widehat{P}_{d,h}(\tau(\Delta q_h))$; multiplying by the non-positive quantity $-\tau(\Delta q_h) = -\alpha\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h)$ reverses the inequality. Conversely, if $\tau(\Delta q_h) < 0$, then $\tau(\Delta q_h) \leq \tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h) < 0$ implies $\widehat{P}_{d,h}(\tau(\Delta q_h)) \leq \widehat{P}_{d,h}(\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h))$; multiplying by the positive quantity $-\tau(\Delta q_h) = -\alpha\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h)$ preserves the inequality. In both cases, we obtain
\begin{align*}
    -\tau(\Delta q_h)\widehat{P}_{d,h}(\tau(\Delta q_h)) - \lambda|\Delta q_h|
    \leq \alpha\left[-\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h)\widehat{P}_{d,h}(\tau(\Delta\widetilde{q}_h)) - \lambda|\Delta\widetilde{q}_h|\right].
\end{align*}
Summing over $h=1,\dots,24$ and taking the maximum over $\Delta\bm{q}$ yields the stated bound.
\end{proof}

