proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
    We verify the Borel measurability of each constituent map in Definition~\ref{defn:depth-restricted-step}. First, the composite action application map $(\bm{m},\bm{c})\mapsto\bm{m}\lhd\bm{c}$ is continuous and hence Borel measurable by Theorem~\ref{thm:composite-application-continuous}. Second, the price--time priority relation $\preceq$ of \eqref{eq:price-time-priority} has a Borel-measurable graph in $O\times O$ because it is defined by Boolean combinations of coordinate equalities and strict inequalities, so the minimum sorting map $\varsigma:\mathscr{T}(O)\to\mathscr{S}(O,\preceq)$ is Borel measurable by Theorem~\ref{thm:minimal-sorting-measurable}. Composing these two maps shows that $(\bm{m},\bm{c})\mapsto\widetilde{\bm{m}}=\varsigma(\bm{m}\lhd\bm{c})$ is jointly Borel measurable.

    Third, on $\mathscr{S}(O,\preceq)$, the side separation operators $\bm{\Pi}_{\mathrm{buy}}$ and $\bm{\Pi}_{\mathrm{sell}}$ are continuous by Proposition~\ref{prop:separation-continuous}. For each side $\kappa\in\{\mathrm{buy},\mathrm{sell}\}$, restricting a tuple $\bm{x}\in\mathscr{S}(U,\preceq^\kappa)$ to the first $100$ indices via $\bm{x}\mapsto\bm{x}[\{1,\dots,100\}]$ and extracting its latent tail via $\bm{x}\mapsto\bm{x}[\operatorname{domain}(\bm{x})\setminus\{1,\dots,100\}]$ are continuous on each fixed-length layer $U^n$ and hence Borel measurable by the standard machinery (Theorem~\ref{thm:the-standard-machinery}), Corollary~\ref{cor:filter}, and Proposition~\ref{prop:characteristic-functions-tuple}. Combining these maps with the continuous retagging maps $\bm{\iota}_\kappa$ (Corollary~\ref{cor:retagging-measurable}) and continuous concatenation $\oplus$ shows that the visible projection $\Pi^{\mathscr{B}}$ and the latent tail maps $\widetilde{\bm{m}}\mapsto\bm{b}^{\mathrm{latent}}$ and $\widetilde{\bm{m}}\mapsto\bm{s}^{\mathrm{latent}}$ are Borel measurable.

    Finally, the clearing operator $\mathsf{C}:\mathscr{S}(O,\preceq)\to\mathscr{S}(O,\preceq)$ is Borel measurable by Theorem~\ref{thm:clearing-measurable}. Since appending the latent tails to the separated sides of $\mathsf{C}(\Pi^{\mathscr{B}}\widetilde{\bm{m}})$ and retagging the resulting buy and sell tuples involve only compositions of $\bm{\Pi}_\kappa$, $\oplus$, and $\bm{\iota}_\kappa$, we conclude that $(\bm{m},\bm{c})\mapsto\bm{m}\unlhd\bm{c}$ is a composition of Borel measurable maps and is therefore jointly Borel measurable on $\mathscr{S}(O,\preceq)\times\mathscr{C}(O)$.
\end{proof}

