proof.rawEnvironment:
\begin{proof}
    We must show that $\Gamma(f)=f$. By Definition~\ref{defn:function}, for each $x\in X$ the pair $(x,f(x))$ is the unique element of $f$ with first coordinate $x$, so $\Gamma(f) = \{(x,f(x)) \mid x \in X\} = \{(x,y) \mid (x,y) \in f\} = f$. The equality therefore follows by the \hyperref[axiom:extensionality]{Axiom of Extensionality}.
\end{proof}

