\begin{prop}\label{prop:empty-domain-function}
    Let $Y$ and $Y^\prime$ be any two sets and let $f:\emptyset \to Y$ and $f^\prime: \emptyset \to Y^\prime$ be functions. Then, $f = f^\prime$.
